{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Terms and patient risk across clinical note types (pre-landmark text)\n",
    "\n",
    "Companion to [13: pathology notes only](13_pathology_topics_vs_risk.ipynb). This notebook reads **Clinician**\n",
    "(`PROGRESS_NOTES.parquet`, which already includes discharge summaries), **Imaging** (`IMAGING_NOTES.parquet`), and\n",
    "**Pathology** (`PATHOLOGY_NOTES.parquet`). Edit `NOTE_TYPES` / `NOTE_PATHS` to choose sources. Missing selected files\n",
    "stop the run rather than silently change it. Run manuscript notebook 04 first for the transferred platinum-trained\n",
    "XGBoost patient risk scores.\n",
    "\n",
    "The primary analysis relates patient TF-IDF weights to continuous raw risk, using Spearman correlation with\n",
    "patient permutations and bootstrap intervals, plus adjusted linear regression. Decile term enrichment, the curated\n",
    "lexicon, and binary term/lexicon associations with risk percentile are supplementary. As in notebook 13, these\n",
    "analyses run on pooled notes. The shared BERTopic model and its pooled / per-type topic analyses\n",
    "moved to [16_clinical_notes_bertopic_vs_risk.ipynb](16_clinical_notes_bertopic_vs_risk.ipynb) on 2026-11-18.\n",
    "\n",
    "All finite scored patients are eligible, including middle-risk patients. No extraction manifest is used or written.\n",
    "The pathology lexicon measures mentions in non-pathology\n",
    "notes too; a mention is not a confirmed diagnosis, and specimen-site inference is not applied to these mixed note types.\n",
    "\n",
    "Aggregate outputs go to `<COMPASS data root>/testing/clinical_notes_topics_vs_risk/`, with prefix `clinical_notes_`:\n",
    "`tfidf_risk_association.csv` and `tfidf_risk_coverage.csv`, plus supplementary term/lexicon enrichment and score associations. Patient IDs and raw notes remain in memory only;\n",
    "no report text is saved. Keep aggregate term tables protected as well.\n",
    "The [Elio extraction](../../patient_extraction/01_high_vs_low_risk_transfer_pxs.ipynb) is a separate notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Timing: pre-landmark text only.** At each landmark, a note is used when its date is at or before ADT + landmark (notes before ADT start are included). Days run from ADT start (`TREATMENT_ANCHOR_DATE` in `DATA_PATH`) to the note's `EVENT_DATE`, dated as in notebook 11. Undated notes and notes dated after ADT + landmark are dropped. The window is applied per landmark, so a note at ADT + 120 d is used at +180 but not at +0 or +90. Outputs go to the `pre_landmark/` subfolder of the output folder. Every selected note type needs `EVENT_DATE`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Associations use only notes written before the landmark, so they cannot reflect later outcomes, but they\n",
    "remain descriptive and do not establish prospective predictive value.\n"
   ],
   "id": "overview"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configuration"
   ],
   "id": "configuration"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, \"../../../pipeline\")\n",
    "import compass_pipeline as cp\n",
    "\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = cp.PROJECT_ROOT\n",
    "for _p in (str(PROJECT_ROOT),):\n",
    "    if _p not in sys.path:\n",
    "        sys.path.insert(0, _p)\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from survival_common import federated_scoring as fs\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_ROOT = Path(cp._PROFILE_OUTPUT_ROOT)\n",
    "RHINO_ROOT = Path(os.environ.get(\"COMPASS_RHINO_ROOT\", str(DATA_ROOT / \"rhino_data_v2\")))\n",
    "\n",
    "# >>> Edit <<<\n",
    "SCORES_PATH = RHINO_ROOT / \"federated_transfer_adt_no_DFCI\" / \"all_models\" / \"transfer_scores.csv\"   # notebook 04\n",
    "NOTES_ROOT = Path(os.environ.get(\"PROFILE_CLINICAL_NOTES\", str(Path(cp._PROFILE_DATA_ROOT) / \"CLINICAL_NOTES\")))\n",
    "NOTE_PATHS = {\n",
    "    \"Clinician\": NOTES_ROOT / \"PROGRESS_NOTES.parquet\",\n",
    "    \"Imaging\": NOTES_ROOT / \"IMAGING_NOTES.parquet\",\n",
    "    \"Pathology\": Path(os.environ.get(\"PROFILE_PATHOLOGY_NOTES\", str(NOTES_ROOT / \"PATHOLOGY_NOTES.parquet\"))),\n",
    "}\n",
    "NOTE_TYPES = (\"Clinician\", \"Imaging\", \"Pathology\")\n",
    "\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR = DATA_ROOT / \"testing\" / \"clinical_notes_topics_vs_risk\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pre-landmark text only: at each landmark, notes with EVENT_DATE <= ADT + landmark (pre-ADT notes included).\n",
    "# Undated notes are dropped. Outputs go to the pre_landmark/ subfolder.\n",
    "DATA_PATH = DATA_ROOT / \"longitudinal_prediction_data_adt.csv\"   # ADT anchor dates (TREATMENT_ANCHOR_DATE)\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR = OUTPUT_DIR / \"pre_landmark\"\n",
    "\n",
    "MODEL_FAMILY = \"xgboost_cox\"\n",
    "SCORE_ENDPOINT = \"platinum\"        # the model is platinum-trained; risk_score is identical across endpoints\n",
    "LANDMARKS = (0, 90, 180)\n",
    "DECILE = 0.10                      # top and bottom 10% at each landmark\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pooled clinical-note term enrichment (top vs bottom decile)\n",
    "TERM_MIN_PATIENTS = 5              # a term must appear in >= this many patients at the landmark\n",
    "TERM_NGRAMS = (1, 2)               # unigrams and bigrams\n",
    "TERM_FDR = 0.05                    # Benjamini-Hochberg threshold for the displayed tables\n",
    "TERM_TOP_N = 25                    # terms shown per landmark x group\n",
    "\n",
    "# Stratified sensitivity tests: report-count band x note-type availability pattern\n",
    "ADJUST_REPORT_BANDS = (1, 2, 4)    # band lower edges: 1, 2-3, 4+ reports\n",
    "\n",
    "# Primary continuous TF-IDF/risk analysis; whole-patient resampling, separately at each landmark.\n",
    "TFIDF_SETTINGS = dict(min_patients=30, min_term_patients=TERM_MIN_PATIENTS,\n",
    "                      n_permutations=9999, n_bootstrap=1000, seed=42, block_size=64)\n"
   ],
   "id": "config"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Risk scores (all patients)\n",
    "\n",
    "One full-model XGBoost score per patient and landmark. Invalid scores are excluded. Decile labels support the legacy\n",
    "contrasts only; coincident cutoffs leave all finite scores in the middle group and do not block continuous analyses.\n"
   ],
   "id": "score-description"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "scores = pd.read_csv(SCORES_PATH, low_memory=False)\n",
    "print(scores.groupby([\"model_family\", \"config\"]).size())\n",
    "\n",
    "sel = scores[(scores[\"model_family\"] == MODEL_FAMILY) & (scores[\"config\"] != \"baseline\")\n",
    "             & (scores[\"endpoint\"] == SCORE_ENDPOINT) & (scores[\"landmark_days\"].isin(LANDMARKS))]\n",
    "sel = sel[[fs.ID_COL, \"landmark_days\", \"risk_score\"]]\n",
    "dup = sel.duplicated([fs.ID_COL, \"landmark_days\"], keep=False)\n",
    "assert not dup.any(), f\"{dup.sum()} rows: more than one {MODEL_FAMILY} model/arm per patient and landmark; narrow the filter above\"\n",
    "assert set(sel[\"landmark_days\"]) == set(LANDMARKS), f\"landmarks found: {sorted(sel['landmark_days'].unique())}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "def decile_flags(g):\n",
    "    if not 0 < DECILE < 0.5:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\"DECILE must be between 0 and 0.5 (exclusive).\")\n",
    "    g = g.copy()\n",
    "    risk = pd.to_numeric(g[\"risk_score\"], errors=\"coerce\").astype(float)\n",
    "    risk = risk.where(np.isfinite(risk))\n",
    "    valid = risk.notna()\n",
    "    landmark = g[\"landmark_days\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "    lo, hi = risk[valid].quantile([DECILE, 1 - DECILE]) if valid.any() else (np.nan, np.nan)\n",
    "    if not valid.any() or lo >= hi:\n",
    "        print(f\"Landmark {landmark}: no distinct decile cutoffs; legacy extreme-group contrasts unavailable.\")\n",
    "    g[\"risk_score\"] = risk\n",
    "    g[\"risk_percentile\"] = risk.rank(pct=True, method=\"average\")\n",
    "    # Only the two extreme deciles are labelled; everything in between stays blank.\n",
    "    g[\"decile_group\"] = pd.Series(pd.NA, index=g.index, dtype=\"string\")\n",
    "    if lo < hi:\n",
    "        g.loc[risk >= hi, \"decile_group\"] = \"top\"\n",
    "        g.loc[risk <= lo, \"decile_group\"] = \"bottom\"\n",
    "    g.loc[~valid, \"decile_group\"] = \"not scored\"\n",
    "    g.attrs.update(lo=lo, hi=hi)\n",
    "    return g\n",
    "\n",
    "by_lm = {lm: decile_flags(g) for lm, g in sel.groupby(\"landmark_days\")}\n",
    "cutoffs = pd.DataFrame({lm: {\"n_scored\": int(g[\"risk_score\"].notna().sum()),\n",
    "                            \"n_not_scored\": int(g[\"risk_score\"].isna().sum()),\n",
    "                            \"bottom_cutoff\": g.attrs[\"lo\"], \"top_cutoff\": g.attrs[\"hi\"],\n",
    "                            \"n_top\": int((g[\"decile_group\"] == \"top\").sum()),\n",
    "                            \"n_bottom\": int((g[\"decile_group\"] == \"bottom\").sum())} for lm, g in by_lm.items()}).T\n",
    "cutoffs"
   ],
   "id": "risk-scores"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pooled clinical-note term enrichment: top vs bottom decile\n",
    "\n",
    "At each landmark, the patients in the **top** and **bottom** deciles of that landmark's score are compared (ties at a\n",
    "cutoff stay in the extreme groups; patients in neither decile are not analysed). Two contrasts per landmark, each reading\n",
    "\"overrepresented in `group` relative to `control`\": top vs bottom and bottom vs top (both directions, because the test\n",
    "is one-sided). Each patient's group can differ between landmarks.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Reports:** the pre-landmark clinical notes of each scored patient (see the overview). Groups come from each\n",
    "  landmark's score. Pre-landmark notes were already on file when the patient was scored, so terms cannot reflect later progression. Patients with no\n",
    "  clinical note in the window drop out of that landmark's denominators.\n",
    "- **Terms:** lowercased letter-only unigrams and bigrams (numbers, dates and IDs drop out), English stop words removed,\n",
    "  counted within each report so bigrams never span two reports. A term is kept if it appears in at least\n",
    "  `TERM_MIN_PATIENTS` patients at the landmark, which reduces rare strings but does not guarantee de-identification; keep outputs protected.\n",
    "- **Test:** a patient \"has\" a term if any of their reports contains it. For each contrast, one-sided Fisher's\n",
    "  exact test for overrepresentation in `group`, Benjamini-Hochberg q-values within each contrast, and the odds ratio\n",
    "  with a +0.5 correction. Mean patient-level TF-IDF (sublinear term frequency over each patient's pooled counts) is reported\n",
    "  for each group as a descriptive column. The `*_mh` columns repeat the test stratified by report count and note-type\n",
    "  availability (Mantel-Haenszel; see below)."
   ],
   "id": "term-description"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "import re\n",
    "\n",
    "import polars as pl\n",
    "\n",
    "TERM_GROUPS = (\"top\", \"bottom\")\n",
    "CONTROL_GROUP = \"middle\"   # patients in neither decile: a label only, never analysed\n",
    "CONTRASTS = ((\"top\", \"bottom\"), (\"bottom\", \"top\"))   # one-sided, so both directions\n",
    "\n",
    "def rpt_key(values):\n",
    "    \"\"\"RPT_ID as a string join key; whole-number IDs lose any float formatting (\"12.0\" -> \"12\").\"\"\"\n",
    "    s = pd.Series(values).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    num = pd.to_numeric(s, errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "    whole = num.notna() & np.isfinite(num) & (num % 1 == 0)\n",
    "    key = s.astype(\"string\").str.strip()\n",
    "    key[whole] = num[whole].astype(\"int64\").astype(str)\n",
    "    return key.where(s.notna())\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def note_keys(frame):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Collision-safe identity across sources/patients; missing report IDs have no embedding join key.\"\"\"\n",
    "    report = rpt_key(frame[\"RPT_ID\"])\n",
    "    patient = rpt_key(frame[\"DFCI_MRN\"])\n",
    "    kind = frame[\"NOTE_TYPE\"].reset_index(drop=True).astype(\"string\")\n",
    "    valid = report.notna() & patient.notna() & kind.notna()\n",
    "    keys = pd.Series(pd.NA, index=range(len(frame)), dtype=\"string\")\n",
    "    keys.loc[valid] = [json.dumps([t, p, r], separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n",
    "                       for t, p, r in zip(kind[valid], patient[valid], report[valid])]\n",
    "    return keys\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def patient_note_strata(reports):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Report-count band x available note types; no pathology specimen heuristics on other note types.\"\"\"\n",
    "    per = reports.groupby(\"DFCI_MRN\").size()\n",
    "    band = np.searchsorted(ADJUST_REPORT_BANDS, per.to_numpy(), side=\"right\") - 1\n",
    "    mask = np.zeros(len(per), dtype=int)\n",
    "    for bit, kind in enumerate(NOTE_TYPES):\n",
    "        ids = reports.loc[reports[\"NOTE_TYPE\"].eq(kind), \"DFCI_MRN\"].unique()\n",
    "        mask += per.index.isin(ids).astype(int) * (2 ** bit)\n",
    "    return pd.Series(band * (2 ** len(NOTE_TYPES)) + mask, index=per.index, name=\"stratum\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def note_views(reports):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Pooled and per-type views using the same report membership and shared topic vocabulary.\"\"\"\n",
    "    yield \"All\", reports\n",
    "    for kind in NOTE_TYPES:\n",
    "        yield kind, reports[reports[\"NOTE_TYPE\"].eq(kind)]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "groups_by_lm = {}\n",
    "for lm, g in by_lm.items():\n",
    "    ids = pd.Index(pd.to_numeric(g[fs.ID_COL], errors=\"coerce\").astype(\"Int64\"), name=\"DFCI_MRN\")\n",
    "    grp = pd.Series(g[\"decile_group\"].fillna(CONTROL_GROUP).to_numpy(), index=ids, name=\"group\")\n",
    "    groups_by_lm[lm] = grp[grp.ne(\"not scored\")]\n",
    "\n",
    "if not NOTE_TYPES or len(set(NOTE_TYPES)) != len(NOTE_TYPES) or \"All\" in NOTE_TYPES:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"Select unique NOTE_TYPES; All is reserved for pooled results.\")\n",
    "scored_ids = sorted({int(i) for grp in groups_by_lm.values() for i in grp.index.dropna()})\n",
    "frames = []\n",
    "for kind in NOTE_TYPES:\n",
    "    path = Path(NOTE_PATHS[kind])\n",
    "    if not path.exists():\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Selected {kind} notes not found: {path}; edit NOTE_TYPES/NOTE_PATHS if intentional.\")\n",
    "    scan = pl.scan_parquet(path)\n",
    "    schema = scan.collect_schema().names()\n",
    "    required = {\"DFCI_MRN\", \"RPT_TEXT\"}\n",
    "    if not required.issubset(schema):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"{kind} notes missing columns: {sorted(required - set(schema))}\")\n",
    "    cols = [c for c in (\"DFCI_MRN\", \"RPT_TEXT\", \"RPT_ID\", \"EVENT_DATE\", \"PROC_DESC\") if c in schema]\n",
    "    frame = (scan.select(cols)\n",
    "             .filter(pl.col(\"DFCI_MRN\").cast(pl.Int64, strict=False).is_in(scored_ids)).collect().to_pandas())\n",
    "    if \"RPT_ID\" not in frame:\n",
    "        frame[\"RPT_ID\"] = pd.NA   # still usable for terms, but cannot join embeddings\n",
    "    if \"EVENT_DATE\" not in frame:\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f\"{kind} notes have no EVENT_DATE; the pre-landmark window needs dated notes.\")\n",
    "    frame[\"NOTE_TYPE\"] = kind\n",
    "    frames.append(frame)\n",
    "all_notes = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True)\n",
    "all_notes[\"DFCI_MRN\"] = pd.to_numeric(all_notes[\"DFCI_MRN\"], errors=\"coerce\").astype(\"Int64\")\n",
    "all_notes[\"RPT_TEXT\"] = all_notes[\"RPT_TEXT\"].fillna(\"\").astype(str)\n",
    "all_notes[\"rpt_key\"] = note_keys(all_notes).to_numpy()\n",
    "all_notes[\"note_date\"] = pd.to_datetime(\n",
    "    all_notes[\"EVENT_DATE\"].astype(\"string\").str.extract(r\"^(\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2})\", expand=False), errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "identified = all_notes[all_notes[\"rpt_key\"].notna()]\n",
    "if identified.groupby(\"rpt_key\")[\"RPT_TEXT\"].nunique().gt(1).any():\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"Conflicting note text for the same note-type/patient/report identity.\")\n",
    "# Reconcile dates before keeping one copy: an undated copy must not hide a dated report.\n",
    "dates = identified.groupby(\"rpt_key\")[\"note_date\"]\n",
    "if dates.nunique().gt(1).any():\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"Conflicting note dates for the same note-type/patient/report identity.\")\n",
    "all_notes.loc[identified.index, \"note_date\"] = dates.transform(\"first\")\n",
    "all_notes = all_notes[all_notes[\"rpt_key\"].isna() | ~all_notes[\"rpt_key\"].duplicated()].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "all_notes[\"note_row\"] = np.arange(len(all_notes))\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Pre-landmark window. Days from ADT start = EVENT_DATE (its YYYY-MM-DD prefix) - TREATMENT_ANCHOR_DATE,\n",
    "# dated as in notebook 11. Undated notes are dropped.\n",
    "anchor_cols = [\"DFCI_MRN\", \"TREATMENT_ANCHOR_DATE\"]\n",
    "anchor = (pd.read_parquet(DATA_PATH, columns=anchor_cols) if str(DATA_PATH).endswith((\".parquet\", \".pq\"))\n",
    "          else pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH, usecols=anchor_cols, low_memory=False)).dropna().drop_duplicates()\n",
    "anchor[\"TREATMENT_ANCHOR_DATE\"] = pd.to_datetime(anchor[\"TREATMENT_ANCHOR_DATE\"], errors=\"coerce\", format=\"mixed\")\n",
    "anchor = anchor.dropna().drop_duplicates()\n",
    "anchor[\"DFCI_MRN\"] = pd.to_numeric(anchor[\"DFCI_MRN\"], errors=\"raise\").astype(\"int64\")\n",
    "if anchor[\"DFCI_MRN\"].duplicated().any():\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"More than one TREATMENT_ANCHOR_DATE for some patients.\")\n",
    "anchor = anchor.set_index(\"DFCI_MRN\")[\"TREATMENT_ANCHOR_DATE\"]\n",
    "n_missing = sum(i not in anchor.index for i in scored_ids)\n",
    "if n_missing:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(f\"{n_missing} scored patients lack an ADT anchor in DATA_PATH; reconcile it with the scores.\")\n",
    "note_date = all_notes[\"note_date\"]\n",
    "all_notes[\"days_from_adt\"] = (note_date - all_notes[\"DFCI_MRN\"].map(anchor)).dt.days.astype(float).to_numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def in_window(reports, lm):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Rows of `reports` dated at or before ADT + `lm`, pre-ADT included (undated rows never).\"\"\"\n",
    "    days = reports[\"days_from_adt\"]\n",
    "    return (days.le(lm)).fillna(False).to_numpy(dtype=bool)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def window_summary(rows):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Prints, per landmark, how many of the scored patients' notes are pre-landmark (aggregate counts only).\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(\"Pre-landmark notes (note date <= ADT + landmark; undated notes dropped):\")\n",
    "    for r in rows:\n",
    "        print(f\"  landmark {r['landmark']}: {r['in_window']:,} of {r['any_date']:,} notes \"\n",
    "              f\"({r['undated']:,} undated), {r['patients_in_window']:,} patients\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# The pre-landmark notes of the patients scored at each landmark.\n",
    "reports_by_lm, strata_by_lm, size_rows, window_rows = {}, {}, [], []\n",
    "for lm, grp in groups_by_lm.items():\n",
    "    pool = all_notes[all_notes[\"DFCI_MRN\"].isin(grp.index)]\n",
    "    rep_lm = pool[in_window(pool, lm)].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    reports_by_lm[lm] = rep_lm\n",
    "    window_rows.append(dict(landmark=lm, any_date=len(pool), in_window=len(rep_lm),\n",
    "                            undated=int(pool[\"days_from_adt\"].isna().sum()),\n",
    "                            patients_in_window=int(rep_lm[\"DFCI_MRN\"].nunique())))\n",
    "    strata_by_lm[lm] = patient_note_strata(rep_lm)\n",
    "    for kind, view in note_views(rep_lm):\n",
    "        per = view.groupby(\"DFCI_MRN\").size()\n",
    "        for name in TERM_GROUPS:\n",
    "            members = grp.index[grp.eq(name).to_numpy()]\n",
    "            counts = per[per.index.isin(members)]\n",
    "            size_rows.append(dict(landmark=lm, note_type=kind, group=name, patients_scored=len(members),\n",
    "                                  patients_with_report=len(counts), reports=int(counts.sum()),\n",
    "                                  median_reports=float(counts.median()) if len(counts) else np.nan))\n",
    "group_sizes = pd.DataFrame(size_rows).set_index([\"landmark\", \"note_type\", \"group\"])\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(all_notes):,} clinical notes across {len(NOTE_TYPES)} selected types (any date, before the window).\")\n",
    "window_summary(window_rows)\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from IPython.display import display\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    display = print\n",
    "display(group_sizes)\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "reports"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "from scipy import sparse\n",
    "from scipy.stats import hypergeom, norm\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer, TfidfTransformer\n",
    "\n",
    "# Applied after lowercasing: letters only, >= 3 characters.\n",
    "TOKEN_PATTERN = r\"(?u)\\b[a-z][a-z]{2,}\\b\"\n",
    "MH_COLS = [\"odds_ratio_mh\", \"p_value_mh\", \"q_value_mh\"]\n",
    "ENRICHMENT_COLS = [\"landmark\", \"group\", \"control\", \"term\", \"n_group\", \"n_control\", \"group_with_term\", \"control_with_term\",\n",
    "                   \"pct_group\", \"pct_control\", \"odds_ratio\", \"p_value\", \"q_value\", *MH_COLS,\n",
    "                   \"mean_tfidf_group\", \"mean_tfidf_control\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def bh_qvalues(p):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Benjamini-Hochberg q-values over the finite p values; NaN stays NaN (cluster scipy predates\n",
    "    false_discovery_control).\"\"\"\n",
    "    p = np.asarray(p, dtype=float)\n",
    "    q = np.full(p.shape, np.nan)\n",
    "    ok = np.flatnonzero(np.isfinite(p))\n",
    "    if ok.size:\n",
    "        order = ok[np.argsort(p[ok])]\n",
    "        ranked = p[order] * ok.size / np.arange(1, ok.size + 1)\n",
    "        q[order] = np.minimum(np.minimum.accumulate(ranked[::-1])[::-1], 1.0)\n",
    "    return q\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def patient_term_matrices(reports, ids):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Patient x term presence and TF-IDF, with terms counted within each report and summed per patient.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    text = reports[\"RPT_TEXT\"].to_numpy()\n",
    "    vec = CountVectorizer(lowercase=True, stop_words=\"english\", token_pattern=TOKEN_PATTERN,\n",
    "                          ngram_range=TERM_NGRAMS, min_df=TERM_MIN_PATIENTS)\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        # Report-level min_df is a safe prefilter: a term in >= k patients is in >= k reports.\n",
    "        counts = vec.fit_transform(text)\n",
    "    except ValueError:  # no term survives (or fewer reports than TERM_MIN_PATIENTS)\n",
    "        return np.array([], dtype=object), None, None\n",
    "    rows = ids.get_indexer(reports[\"DFCI_MRN\"])\n",
    "    to_patient = sparse.csr_matrix((np.ones(len(rows)), (rows, np.arange(len(rows)))),\n",
    "                                   shape=(len(ids), len(rows)))\n",
    "    patient_counts = (to_patient @ counts).tocsc()\n",
    "    present = (patient_counts > 0).astype(np.int64)\n",
    "    keep = np.flatnonzero(np.asarray(present.sum(axis=0)).ravel() >= TERM_MIN_PATIENTS)\n",
    "    if not keep.size:\n",
    "        return np.array([], dtype=object), None, None\n",
    "    patient_counts, present = patient_counts[:, keep], present[:, keep]\n",
    "    tfidf = TfidfTransformer(sublinear_tf=True).fit_transform(patient_counts)\n",
    "    return vec.get_feature_names_out()[keep], present.tocsr(), tfidf.tocsr()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def colsum(m):\n",
    "    return np.asarray(m.sum(axis=0)).ravel().astype(float)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def mantel_haenszel(present, in_group, control, strata):\n",
    "    \"\"\"One-sided, continuity-corrected Mantel-Haenszel test and MH odds ratio per feature column, across strata.\n",
    "\n",
    "    A stratum without patients from both sides carries no information and is skipped; if none is left, both are NaN.\n",
    "    The odds ratio adds 0.5 to every cell of a stratum that has an empty cell.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    n_feat = present.shape[1]\n",
    "    A, E, V, R, S = (np.zeros(n_feat) for _ in range(5))\n",
    "    informative = False\n",
    "    for k in pd.unique(strata[in_group | control]):\n",
    "        g, c = in_group & (strata == k), control & (strata == k)\n",
    "        n1, n0 = int(g.sum()), int(c.sum())\n",
    "        if not (n1 and n0):\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        informative = True\n",
    "        n = n1 + n0\n",
    "        a, cc = colsum(present[g]), colsum(present[c])\n",
    "        b, d, m = n1 - a, n0 - cc, a + cc\n",
    "        A += a\n",
    "        E += n1 * m / n\n",
    "        V += n1 * n0 * m * (n - m) / (n ** 2 * (n - 1))\n",
    "        h = 0.5 * ((a == 0) | (b == 0) | (cc == 0) | (d == 0))\n",
    "        R += (a + h) * (d + h) / (n + 4 * h)\n",
    "        S += (b + h) * (cc + h) / (n + 4 * h)\n",
    "    if not informative:\n",
    "        return np.full(n_feat, np.nan), np.full(n_feat, np.nan)\n",
    "    with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\", invalid=\"ignore\"):\n",
    "        p = np.where(V > 0, norm.sf((A - E - 0.5) / np.sqrt(V)), 1.0)\n",
    "    return R / S, p\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fisher_enrichment(present, label, features, landmark, strata=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"One-sided Fisher overrepresentation of each feature column for each (group, control) in CONTRASTS.\n",
    "\n",
    "    present: patients x features 0/1 sparse matrix; label: each patient's group; strata (optional): each patient's\n",
    "    stratum for the Mantel-Haenszel columns (NaN without it). Rows come out in CONTRASTS order, len(features) rows\n",
    "    per contrast whose group and control both have patients.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    out = []\n",
    "    for name, ref in CONTRASTS:\n",
    "        in_group, control = label == name, label == ref\n",
    "        n1, n0 = int(in_group.sum()), int(control.sum())\n",
    "        if n1 == 0 or n0 == 0:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        a, c = colsum(present[in_group]), colsum(present[control])\n",
    "        p = hypergeom.sf(a - 1, n1 + n0, a + c, n1)       # P(X >= a): one-sided Fisher\n",
    "        if strata is None:\n",
    "            or_mh = p_mh = np.full(len(features), np.nan)\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            or_mh, p_mh = mantel_haenszel(present, in_group, control, np.asarray(strata))\n",
    "        out.append(pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "            \"landmark\": landmark, \"group\": name, \"control\": ref, \"feature\": features, \"n_group\": n1, \"n_control\": n0,\n",
    "            \"group_with_feature\": a.astype(int), \"control_with_feature\": c.astype(int),\n",
    "            \"pct_group\": a / n1, \"pct_control\": c / n0,\n",
    "            \"odds_ratio\": ((a + 0.5) * (n0 - c + 0.5)) / ((n1 - a + 0.5) * (c + 0.5)),\n",
    "            \"p_value\": p, \"q_value\": bh_qvalues(p),\n",
    "            \"odds_ratio_mh\": or_mh, \"p_value_mh\": p_mh, \"q_value_mh\": bh_qvalues(p_mh),\n",
    "        }))\n",
    "    return pd.concat(out, ignore_index=True) if out else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def sort_contrasts(df):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Landmark, then CONTRASTS order, then p value and odds ratio.\"\"\"\n",
    "    rank = {pair: i for i, pair in enumerate(CONTRASTS)}\n",
    "    order = pd.Series([rank[pair] for pair in zip(df[\"group\"], df[\"control\"])], index=df.index, dtype=float)\n",
    "    return (df.assign(_contrast=order)\n",
    "            .sort_values([\"landmark\", \"_contrast\", \"p_value\", \"odds_ratio\"], ascending=[True, True, True, False])\n",
    "            .drop(columns=\"_contrast\").reset_index(drop=True))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def contrast_title(lm, name, ref):\n",
    "    return f\"Landmark {lm} · {name} decile vs {ref} decile\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "term_matrices = {}   # landmark -> (patient ids, terms, presence, TF-IDF); reused by the score association cell\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def term_enrichment(reports, groups, landmark):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Fisher overrepresentation of each term for each contrast in CONTRASTS at one landmark.\"\"\"\n",
    "    ids = pd.Index(sorted(reports[\"DFCI_MRN\"].unique()), dtype=\"Int64\")   # patients with >= 1 report\n",
    "    terms, present, tfidf = patient_term_matrices(reports, ids)\n",
    "    term_matrices[landmark] = (ids, terms, present, tfidf)\n",
    "    if not len(terms):\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame(columns=ENRICHMENT_COLS)\n",
    "    label = groups.reindex(ids).to_numpy()\n",
    "    res = fisher_enrichment(present, label, terms, landmark, strata_by_lm[landmark].reindex(ids).to_numpy())\n",
    "    if res.empty:\n",
    "        return pd.DataFrame(columns=ENRICHMENT_COLS)\n",
    "    mean_tfidf = {name: np.asarray(tfidf[label == name].mean(axis=0)).ravel()\n",
    "                  for name in set(res[\"group\"]) | set(res[\"control\"])}\n",
    "    pairs = list(res[[\"group\", \"control\"]].drop_duplicates().itertuples(index=False))\n",
    "    res[\"mean_tfidf_group\"] = np.concatenate([mean_tfidf[g] for g, _ in pairs])\n",
    "    res[\"mean_tfidf_control\"] = np.concatenate([mean_tfidf[c] for _, c in pairs])\n",
    "    return res.rename(columns={\"feature\": \"term\", \"group_with_feature\": \"group_with_term\",\n",
    "                               \"control_with_feature\": \"control_with_term\"})\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "enrichment = pd.concat(\n",
    "    [term_enrichment(reports_by_lm[lm], groups_by_lm[lm], lm) for lm in LANDMARKS if lm in reports_by_lm],\n",
    "    ignore_index=True,\n",
    ").reindex(columns=ENRICHMENT_COLS)\n",
    "enrichment = sort_contrasts(enrichment)\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "enrichment_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"clinical_notes_term_enrichment.csv\"\n",
    "enrichment.to_csv(enrichment_path, index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"wrote {enrichment_path} ({len(enrichment):,} term x contrast rows)\")\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "id": "term-enrichment"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "tfidf-continuous-description",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Primary analysis: continuous TF-IDF and patient risk\n",
    "\n",
    "Every eligible patient contributes their continuous raw risk score and one TF-IDF vector; decile labels do not\n",
    "enter this analysis. We reuse the vocabulary and patient-level TF-IDF fitted separately within each landmark.\n",
    "Weights are zero when the term is absent. Positive effects indicate increasing relative term prominence with risk;\n",
    "these weights are not absolute mention counts or measures of disease severity.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Primary: Spearman rho.** A rank correlation between raw risk and each term's TF-IDF weight. Ties, including\n",
    "  zero weights, receive average ranks. Two-sided patient permutations test an independence null by shuffling scores\n",
    "  between patients, with each patient's complete vector kept together. This is an unadjusted descriptive association.\n",
    "  Paired patient bootstrap samples are re-ranked to obtain percentile 95% intervals, conditional on the fitted\n",
    "  vocabulary and IDF. Constant bootstrap samples are omitted; intervals are withheld if fewer than 80% of samples\n",
    "  are usable. `n_bootstrap_valid` and `ci_status` report this explicitly.\n",
    "- **Sensitivity: adjusted linear regression.** TF-IDF weight is the response; raw risk is standardized across eligible\n",
    "  patients within the landmark. `beta_per_sd` is the change in mean weight per one SD higher risk. Adjustment includes log(1 + report count) and patient note-type fractions, omitting the first sorted type as reference.\n",
    "  HC3 heteroskedasticity-robust standard errors and residual-df t inference provide p-values and 95% intervals.\n",
    "  Constant covariates are omitted; collinear or unstable designs are marked as skipped. This is a linear descriptive\n",
    "  sensitivity analysis; adjustment does not establish causality.\n",
    "- **Inference and coverage.** Require `TFIDF_SETTINGS['min_patients']` patients and\n",
    "  `TFIDF_SETTINGS['min_term_patients']` patients mentioning a term. Invalid scores are excluded; constant scores\n",
    "  or term weights are skipped. BH correction covers all tested terms and landmarks within each method, separately\n",
    "  in each notebook/timing folder. Landmarks share patients and do not constitute independent replication.\n",
    "  The minimum permutation p-value is `1 / (n_permutations + 1)`; increase permutations if this resolution limits FDR\n",
    "  discoveries. Term blocks bound memory use; all blocks use the same patient resampling draws.\n",
    "\n",
    "Aggregate effects go to `clinical_notes_tfidf_risk_association.csv`, with one row per term, landmark and method;\n",
    "`clinical_notes_tfidf_risk_coverage.csv` records patient and vocabulary coverage. No IDs or raw text are exported.\n",
    "Decile enrichment and binary term/lexicon associations below remain supplementary analyses.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "tfidf-continuous",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from COMPASS.multivariable_models import text_tfidf_association as tfa\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from IPython.display import display\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    display = print\n",
    "\n",
    "tfidf_frames, tfidf_coverage = [], []\n",
    "for lm in LANDMARKS:\n",
    "    g = by_lm[lm]\n",
    "    risk = pd.Series(g[\"risk_score\"].to_numpy(dtype=float),\n",
    "                     index=pd.Index(pd.to_numeric(g[fs.ID_COL], errors=\"raise\").astype(\"Int64\")))\n",
    "    entry = term_matrices.get(lm)\n",
    "    tfidf_coverage.append(dict(landmark=lm, patients_scored=int(np.isfinite(risk).sum()),\n",
    "        patients_with_report=reports_by_lm[lm][\"DFCI_MRN\"].nunique(),\n",
    "        n_terms=0 if entry is None else len(entry[1])))\n",
    "    if entry is None or not len(entry[1]):\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    ids, terms, _, tfidf = entry\n",
    "    covariates = tfa.patient_covariates(reports_by_lm[lm], ids, scope=\"clinical_notes\")\n",
    "    tfidf_frames.append(tfa.continuous_tfidf_association(\n",
    "        tfidf, ids, terms, risk, covariates, lm, **TFIDF_SETTINGS))\n",
    "\n",
    "tfidf_association = tfa.adjust_fdr(tfidf_frames)\n",
    "tfidf_association.to_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"clinical_notes_tfidf_risk_association.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "pd.DataFrame(tfidf_coverage).to_csv(OUTPUT_DIR / \"clinical_notes_tfidf_risk_coverage.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"Continuous TF-IDF/risk: {len(tfidf_association):,} term x landmark x method rows; \"\n",
    "      f\"permutation p-value resolution {1 / (TFIDF_SETTINGS['n_permutations'] + 1):.3g}\")\n",
    "display(pd.DataFrame(tfidf_coverage))\n",
    "for method in (\"spearman\", \"ols_adjusted\"):\n",
    "    sub = tfidf_association[tfidf_association[\"method\"].eq(method)]\n",
    "    print(f\"{method}: {sub['status'].eq('ok').sum():,} estimated; \"\n",
    "          f\"{sub['q_value'].lt(TERM_FDR).sum():,} at q < {TERM_FDR} across terms and landmarks\")\n",
    "    effect = \"spearman_rho\" if method == \"spearman\" else \"beta_per_sd\"\n",
    "    for direction, mask in ((\"higher\", sub[effect].gt(0)), (\"lower\", sub[effect].lt(0))):\n",
    "        print(f\"  Terms with {direction} prominence as risk increases:\")\n",
    "        display(sub[mask].sort_values(\"p_value\")[\n",
    "            [\"landmark\", \"term\", \"n_patients\", \"prevalence\", effect, \"ci95_low\", \"ci95_high\",\n",
    "             \"p_value\", \"q_value\", \"ci_status\"]].head(TERM_TOP_N).round(4).reset_index(drop=True))\n",
    "    if sub.empty:\n",
    "        print(\"  No retained vocabulary to test.\")\n",
    "    elif sub['status'].ne('ok').any():\n",
    "        display(sub.loc[sub['status'].ne('ok'), 'status'].value_counts().rename(\"skipped_terms\"))\n"
   ]
  },
