   "source": [
    "## Sensitivity and complementary analyses\n",
    "\n",
    "Pooled selected note types; same groups, landmarks and pre-landmark notes as the term enrichment. Each one addresses a specific way the term\n",
    "tables can mislead.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Report count and note-type availability (`*_mh` columns).** Each patient's stratum is their report-count\n",
    "   band (`ADJUST_REPORT_BANDS`) crossed with which selected note types they have. Here every analysis uses all\n",
    "   reports in the window (notebook 16's topic contrasts recompute it within each embedded-note subset). The term and lexicon\n",
    "   tables add a one-sided, continuity-corrected Mantel-Haenszel test and MH odds ratio across strata.\n",
    "   These are NaN when no stratum contains patients from both sides of the contrast. No specimen-site heuristic\n",
    "   is applied to clinician or imaging text.\n",
    "2. **Curated lexicon (`clinical_notes_lexicon_enrichment.csv`).** The neuroendocrine patterns are copied from the NEPC\n",
    "   annotation pipeline's `ne_gate.py`, joined by individual NE and prostate IHC markers, histologic variants, invasion\n",
    "   / extension terms and the highest Gleason sum (grade group mapped to a sum). Same Fisher and MH tests.\n",
    "3. **Continuous risk (`clinical_notes_score_association.csv`).** Deciles discard most of the score. For every term and\n",
    "   lexicon feature, a two-sided Mann-Whitney test of the risk percentile among all scored patients with a\n",
    "   report, feature present vs absent. `auc` = P(a patient with the feature ranks higher than one without). The van\n",
    "   Elteren test (`*_adj`) stratifies it like item 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "All outputs are aggregate. No MRN or report text is printed or written by these cells."
   ],
   "id": "sensitivity-description"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Curated lexicon, matched on lowercased report text. The NE patterns are copied verbatim (not imported) from\n",
    "# LLM_clinical_annotations/tasks/nepc/ne_gate.py (NE_GATE_VERSION \"ne-gate-v3\", commit\n",
    "# edb1713ef454f6ece313fa675b5f9438937f831e); update them by hand if that file changes.\n",
    "NE_TERM = (r\"\\b(?:neuro[\\s-]?endocrine|t-?nepc|nepc|small[\\s-]?cell|scpc|scnc|\"\n",
    "           r\"oat[\\s-]?cell)\\b\")\n",
    "SMALL_CELL_TERM = r\"\\b(?:small[\\s-]?cell|scpc|scnc|oat[\\s-]?cell)\\b\"\n",
    "NE_DIAGNOSIS = (r\"\\b(?:t-?nepc|nepc|scpc|scnc)\\b|\"\n",
    "                r\"\\b(?:neuro[\\s-]?endocrine|small[\\s-]?cell|oat[\\s-]?cell)\"\n",
    "                r\"(?:\\s+[\\w/()-]+){0,4}?\\s+\"\n",
    "                r\"(?:carcinoma|cancer|tumou?r|neoplasm|malignancy|component|histology|\"\n",
    "                r\"variant|subtype|type|disease|prostate)\\b|\"\n",
    "                r\"\\b(?:carcinoma|cancer)\\s+(?:with|of)\\s+(?:\\w+\\s+){0,2}?\"\n",
    "                r\"(?:neuro[\\s-]?endocrine|small[\\s-]?cell)\\b\")\n",
    "NE_MARKER = (r\"\\b(?:synaptophysin|chromogranin(?:\\s+a)?|cd\\s?56|insm-?1|\"\n",
    "             r\"neuron[\\s-]+specific\\s+enolase|nse)\\b\")\n",
    "NON_PROSTATE_NE = (r\"\\b(?:sclc|small[\\s-]?cell\\s+lung|merkel|carcinoid|\"\n",
    "                   r\"pulmonary\\s+(?:origin|primary|small)|lung\\s+(?:origin|primary)|\"\n",
    "                   r\"urothelial|bladder\\s+(?:primary|origin|cancer|carcinoma|tumou?r)|\"\n",
    "                   r\"pancreatic\\s+(?:net|neuroendocrine)|pnet|gep[\\s-]?nets?|\"\n",
    "                   r\"well[\\s-]differentiated\\s+neuroendocrine\\s+tumou?r)\\b\")\n",
    "NON_SMALL_CELL = r\"\\bnon[\\s-]*$\"\n",
    "# (end of the ne_gate.py copy)\n",
    "\n",
    "LEXICON = {\n",
    "    # neuroendocrine (ne_gate.py), then each NE marker from NE_MARKER on its own\n",
    "    \"NE term (any)\": NE_TERM,\n",
    "    \"NE diagnosis phrase\": NE_DIAGNOSIS,\n",
    "    \"small cell\": SMALL_CELL_TERM,\n",
    "    \"NE marker (any)\": NE_MARKER,\n",
    "    \"non-prostate NE primary\": NON_PROSTATE_NE,\n",
    "    \"synaptophysin\": r\"\\bsynaptophysin\\b\",\n",
    "    \"chromogranin\": r\"\\bchromogranin\\b\",\n",
    "    \"CD56\": r\"\\bcd\\s?56\\b\",\n",
    "    \"INSM1\": r\"\\binsm-?1\\b\",\n",
    "    \"NSE\": r\"\\b(?:neuron[\\s-]+specific\\s+enolase|nse)\\b\",\n",
    "    # other IHC\n",
    "    \"Ki-67 / MIB-1\": r\"\\b(?:ki-?67|mib-?1)\\b\",\n",
    "    \"AR\": r\"\\b(?:androgen\\s+receptor|ar)\\b\",\n",
    "    \"NKX3.1\": r\"\\bnkx\\s?3[.\\s-]?1\\b\",\n",
    "    \"PSMA\": r\"\\b(?:psma|prostate[\\s-]specific\\s+membrane\\s+antigen)\\b\",\n",
    "    \"ERG\": r\"\\berg\\b\",\n",
    "    \"PTEN\": r\"\\bpten\\b\",\n",
    "    # histology and staging\n",
    "    \"ductal\": r\"\\bductal\\b\",\n",
    "    \"intraductal\": r\"\\bintraductal\\b|\\bidc-?p\\b\",\n",
    "    \"cribriform\": r\"\\bcribriform\\b\",\n",
    "    \"sarcomatoid\": r\"\\bsarcomatoid\\b\",\n",
    "    \"treatment effect\": r\"\\b(?:treatment|therapy|hormon\\w*|androgen[\\s-]deprivation)[\\s-]+(?:related\\s+)?effects?\\b\",\n",
    "    \"perineural invasion\": r\"\\bperineural\\s+(?:invasion|infiltration)\\b|\\bpni\\b\",\n",
    "    \"lymphovascular invasion\": (r\"\\b(?:lympho-?vascular|angiolymphatic|lymphatic|vascular)\\s+(?:space\\s+)?invasion\\b\"\n",
    "                                r\"|\\blvi\\b\"),\n",
    "    \"extraprostatic extension\": r\"\\bextra-?prostatic\\s+extension\\b|\\bepe\\b\",\n",
    "    \"seminal vesicle invasion\": r\"\\bseminal\\s+vesicles?\\s+(?:invasion|involvement|involved)\\b|\\bsvi\\b\",\n",
    "}\n",
    "LEXICON_RE = {name: re.compile(rx) for name, rx in LEXICON.items()}\n",
    "NON_PREFIX_RE = re.compile(NON_SMALL_CELL)\n",
    "# Gleason: the highest primary + secondary sum in any report (grade group mapped to a sum).\n",
    "GLEASON_RE = re.compile(r\"\\bgleason\\b[^.;\\n]{0,40}?\\b([1-5])\\s*\\+\\s*([1-5])\\b\")\n",
    "GRADE_GROUP_RE = re.compile(r\"\\b(?:grade\\s+group|isup\\s+grade(?:\\s+group)?|gg)\\s*:?\\s*([1-5])\\b\")\n",
    "GRADE_GROUP_SUM = {1: 6, 2: 7, 3: 7, 4: 8, 5: 9}\n",
    "GLEASON_BINS = ((\"Gleason max 2-6\", 2, 6), (\"Gleason max 7\", 7, 7), (\"Gleason max 8-10\", 8, 10))\n",
    "\n",
    "MENTION_FEATURES = list(LEXICON)\n",
    "LEXICON_FEATURES = MENTION_FEATURES + [label for label, _, _ in GLEASON_BINS]\n",
    "LEXICON_COLS = [\"landmark\", \"group\", \"control\", \"feature\", \"n_group\", \"n_control\", \"group_with_feature\",\n",
    "                \"control_with_feature\", \"pct_group\", \"pct_control\", \"odds_ratio\", \"p_value\", \"q_value\", *MH_COLS]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def lexicon_hits(text):\n",
    "    \"\"\"One report's lexicon features: {feature: True} for each mention, plus gleason_max.\n",
    "\n",
    "    A match right after \"non-\" (\"non-small cell\") is not a mention.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    text = text.lower()\n",
    "    hits = {}\n",
    "    for name, rx in LEXICON_RE.items():\n",
    "        if any(not NON_PREFIX_RE.search(text[max(0, m.start() - 8):m.start()]) for m in rx.finditer(text)):\n",
    "            hits[name] = True\n",
    "    sums = ([int(a) + int(b) for a, b in GLEASON_RE.findall(text)]\n",
    "            + [GRADE_GROUP_SUM[int(g)] for g in GRADE_GROUP_RE.findall(text)])\n",
    "    if sums:\n",
    "        hits[\"gleason_max\"] = max(sums)\n",
    "    return hits\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Report-level hits, once for every report at any landmark.\n",
    "report_rows = np.unique(np.concatenate([rep[\"note_row\"].to_numpy() for rep in reports_by_lm.values()]\n",
    "                                       + [np.array([], dtype=int)])).astype(int)\n",
    "report_lex = pd.DataFrame([lexicon_hits(t) for t in all_notes[\"RPT_TEXT\"].to_numpy()[report_rows]],\n",
    "                          index=report_rows).reindex(columns=MENTION_FEATURES + [\"gleason_max\"])\n",
    "report_mentions = report_lex[MENTION_FEATURES].notna().to_numpy()\n",
    "report_gleason = pd.to_numeric(report_lex[\"gleason_max\"], errors=\"coerce\").to_numpy(dtype=float)\n",
    "lexicon_matrices = {}   # landmark -> (patient ids, presence); reused by the score association cell\n",
    "lexicon_frames = []\n",
    "for lm in LANDMARKS:\n",
    "    if lm not in reports_by_lm or reports_by_lm[lm].empty:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    rep = reports_by_lm[lm]\n",
    "    ids = pd.Index(sorted(rep[\"DFCI_MRN\"].unique()), dtype=\"Int64\")\n",
    "    rows = ids.get_indexer(rep[\"DFCI_MRN\"])\n",
    "    pos = np.searchsorted(report_rows, rep[\"note_row\"].to_numpy())\n",
    "    mentions = np.zeros((len(ids), len(MENTION_FEATURES)), dtype=bool)\n",
    "    np.logical_or.at(mentions, rows, report_mentions[pos])\n",
    "    gleason = np.full(len(ids), np.nan)\n",
    "    np.fmax.at(gleason, rows, report_gleason[pos])\n",
    "    bins = np.column_stack([(gleason >= lo) & (gleason <= hi) for _, lo, hi in GLEASON_BINS])\n",
    "    present = sparse.csr_matrix(np.hstack([mentions, bins]).astype(np.int64))\n",
    "    lexicon_matrices[lm] = (ids, present)\n",
    "    # Only features some patient has at this landmark are tested, so absent ones do not dilute the BH correction.\n",
    "    seen = np.flatnonzero(colsum(present) > 0)\n",
    "    lexicon_frames.append(fisher_enrichment(present[:, seen], groups_by_lm[lm].reindex(ids).to_numpy(),\n",
    "                                            np.array(LEXICON_FEATURES, dtype=object)[seen], lm,\n",
    "                                            strata_by_lm[lm].reindex(ids).to_numpy()))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Rows stay in landmark, CONTRASTS, then LEXICON_FEATURES order.\n",
    "lexicon_enrich = (pd.concat(lexicon_frames, ignore_index=True) if lexicon_frames else pd.DataFrame()\n",
    "                  ).reindex(columns=LEXICON_COLS)\n",
    "OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "lexicon_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"clinical_notes_lexicon_enrichment.csv\"\n",
    "lexicon_enrich.to_csv(lexicon_path, index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"wrote {lexicon_path} ({len(lexicon_enrich):,} feature x contrast rows)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# One wide table per landmark: % of patients with each feature by group, then q values for every contrast\n",
    "# (q = Fisher, q_mh = stratified Mantel-Haenszel). Features no patient has at that landmark are not tested.\n",
    "for lm in LANDMARKS:\n",
    "    sub = lexicon_enrich[lexicon_enrich[\"landmark\"] == lm]\n",
    "    if sub.empty:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\nLandmark {lm} · lexicon: no patients with clinical notes\")\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    wide = pd.DataFrame(index=pd.Index(LEXICON_FEATURES, name=\"feature\"))\n",
    "    for name, ref in CONTRASTS:\n",
    "        c = sub[(sub[\"group\"] == name) & (sub[\"control\"] == ref)].set_index(\"feature\")\n",
    "        if c.empty:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        wide[f\"% {name}\"], wide[f\"% {ref}\"] = c[\"pct_group\"] * 100, c[\"pct_control\"] * 100\n",
    "        wide[f\"q {name}>{ref}\"], wide[f\"q_mh {name}>{ref}\"] = c[\"q_value\"], c[\"q_value_mh\"]\n",
    "    pct_cols = [f\"% {g}\" for g in TERM_GROUPS if f\"% {g}\" in wide]\n",
    "    q_cols = [col for prefix in (\"q \", \"q_mh \") for col in wide.columns if col.startswith(prefix)]\n",
    "    wide = wide[pct_cols + q_cols]\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nLandmark {lm} · curated lexicon (% of patients with a mention in any report)\")\n",
    "    display(wide.dropna(how=\"all\").round(3))\n"
   ],
   "id": "lexicon"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from scipy.stats import rankdata\n",
    "\n",
    "ASSOC_COLS = [\"landmark\", \"feature_set\", \"feature\", \"n_patients\", \"n_with_feature\", \"pct_with_feature\",\n",
    "              \"mean_percentile_with\", \"mean_percentile_without\", \"auc\", \"p_value\", \"q_value\",\n",
    "              \"auc_adj\", \"p_value_adj\", \"q_value_adj\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def _mann_whitney_parts(present, score):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Per feature column: n with it, U of the with-feature patients, and the tie-corrected null variance of U.\"\"\"\n",
    "    n = present.shape[0]\n",
    "    ranks = rankdata(score)\n",
    "    n1 = colsum(present)\n",
    "    u = np.asarray(present.T @ ranks).ravel() - n1 * (n1 + 1) / 2\n",
    "    _, t = np.unique(score, return_counts=True)\n",
    "    ties = float((t.astype(float) ** 3 - t).sum()) / (n * (n - 1)) if n > 1 else 0.0\n",
    "    var = n1 * (n - n1) / 12 * ((n + 1) - ties)\n",
    "    return n1, u, var\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def score_association(present, features, score, strata, landmark, feature_set):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Two-sided Mann-Whitney of the risk percentile, feature present vs absent, among all scored patients with\n",
    "    clinical notes; and the van Elteren test stratified like the Mantel-Haenszel columns.\n",
    "\n",
    "    auc = P(percentile of a patient with the feature > one without); auc_adj pools the same comparison within strata.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    present = present.tocsr().astype(float)\n",
    "    n = present.shape[0]\n",
    "    n1, u, var = _mann_whitney_parts(present, score)\n",
    "    n0 = n - n1\n",
    "    with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\", invalid=\"ignore\"):\n",
    "        z = np.maximum(np.abs(u - n1 * n0 / 2) - 0.5, 0) / np.sqrt(var)\n",
    "        p = np.where(var > 0, 2 * norm.sf(z), np.nan)\n",
    "        sum_with = np.asarray(present.T @ score).ravel()\n",
    "        res = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "            \"landmark\": landmark, \"feature_set\": feature_set, \"feature\": features, \"n_patients\": n,\n",
    "            \"n_with_feature\": n1.astype(int), \"pct_with_feature\": n1 / n,\n",
    "            \"mean_percentile_with\": sum_with / n1, \"mean_percentile_without\": (score.sum() - sum_with) / n0,\n",
    "            \"auc\": u / (n1 * n0), \"p_value\": p})\n",
    "    # van Elteren: within-stratum U, strata weighted 1 / (N_k + 1).\n",
    "    num, den, u_pool, pairs = (np.zeros(len(features)) for _ in range(4))\n",
    "    for k in pd.unique(strata):\n",
    "        rows = np.flatnonzero(strata == k)\n",
    "        if rows.size < 2:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        n1k, uk, vk = _mann_whitney_parts(present[rows], score[rows])\n",
    "        w = 1 / (rows.size + 1)\n",
    "        num += w * (uk - n1k * (rows.size - n1k) / 2)\n",
    "        den += w ** 2 * vk\n",
    "        u_pool += uk\n",
    "        pairs += n1k * (rows.size - n1k)\n",
    "    with np.errstate(divide=\"ignore\", invalid=\"ignore\"):\n",
    "        res[\"auc_adj\"] = np.where(pairs > 0, u_pool / pairs, np.nan)\n",
    "        res[\"p_value_adj\"] = np.where(den > 0, 2 * norm.sf(np.abs(num) / np.sqrt(den)), np.nan)\n",
    "    res = res[(res[\"n_with_feature\"] > 0) & (res[\"n_with_feature\"] < n)].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "    res[\"q_value\"], res[\"q_value_adj\"] = bh_qvalues(res[\"p_value\"]), bh_qvalues(res[\"p_value_adj\"])\n",
    "    return res[ASSOC_COLS]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "assoc_frames = []\n",
    "for lm in LANDMARKS:\n",
    "    if lm not in by_lm:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    g = by_lm[lm]\n",
    "    pct = pd.Series(g[\"risk_percentile\"].to_numpy(dtype=float),\n",
    "                    index=pd.Index(pd.to_numeric(g[fs.ID_COL], errors=\"coerce\").astype(\"Int64\")))\n",
    "    sets = []\n",
    "    if lm in term_matrices and len(term_matrices[lm][1]):\n",
    "        ids, terms, present, _ = term_matrices[lm]\n",
    "        sets.append((\"term\", ids, present, terms))\n",
    "    if lm in lexicon_matrices:\n",
    "        ids, present = lexicon_matrices[lm]\n",
    "        sets.append((\"lexicon\", ids, present, np.array(LEXICON_FEATURES, dtype=object)))\n",
    "    for feature_set, ids, present, names in sets:\n",
    "        if len(ids) < 2:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        assoc_frames.append(score_association(present, names, pct.reindex(ids).to_numpy(dtype=float),\n",
    "                                              strata_by_lm[lm].reindex(ids).to_numpy(), lm, feature_set))\n",
    "\n",
    "assoc = (pd.concat(assoc_frames, ignore_index=True) if assoc_frames else pd.DataFrame()).reindex(columns=ASSOC_COLS)\n",
    "assoc_path = OUTPUT_DIR / \"clinical_notes_score_association.csv\"\n",
    "assoc.to_csv(assoc_path, index=False)\n",
    "print(f\"wrote {assoc_path} ({len(assoc):,} feature x landmark rows)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "assoc_show = [\"feature\", \"n_with_feature\", \"pct_with_feature\", \"mean_percentile_with\", \"mean_percentile_without\",\n",
    "              \"auc\", \"q_value\", \"auc_adj\", \"q_value_adj\"]\n",
    "for lm in LANDMARKS:\n",
    "    for feature_set in (\"term\", \"lexicon\"):\n",
    "        sub = assoc[(assoc[\"landmark\"] == lm) & (assoc[\"feature_set\"] == feature_set)]\n",
    "        if sub.empty:\n",
    "            print(f\"\\nLandmark {lm} · {feature_set}s vs risk percentile: none tested\")\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        for direction, side in ((\"higher\", sub[\"auc\"] > 0.5), (\"lower\", sub[\"auc\"] < 0.5)):\n",
    "            hits = sub[side].sort_values(\"p_value\")\n",
    "            print(f\"\\nLandmark {lm} · {feature_set}s with {direction} risk percentiles \"\n",
    "                  f\"(q < {TERM_FDR}: {int((hits['q_value'] < TERM_FDR).sum()):,}; top {TERM_TOP_N} by p)\")\n",
    "            display(hits[assoc_show].head(TERM_TOP_N).round(3).reset_index(drop=True))\n"
   ],
   "id": "score-association"
  }
 ],
